# ============================================================
# MPE root .gitignore
# Repo root contains: v15S/  tools/  reference_materials/  run_all.sh  verify.sh
# (DESPOT-2026-10-01: was stale "v15R3/ fixes/ (retired)".)
# ============================================================

# ============ Build output (matches anywhere in tree) ============
*.o
*.d
*.obj
*.a
*.lib
*.so
*.dll
*.exe
engine
mpe-tui
mpe-tui.d
test_*
build/
.fixes_generation_1/
# DESPOT-FIX: was `reference_materials/` — that ignored the 12-file 19MB
# collision/solver/textbook reference library (Coumans/Gottschalk/Mirtich/
# Baraff/Catto/Teschner), risking untracked loss of the audit's own sources.
# Build outputs are already covered by *.o/*.so/build/ above; references stay
# tracked.

# ============ Fix-script backups ============
# Every fix script creates .pre_NNN backups before mutating
*.pre_*

# ============ Backup / scratch files ============
*.bak
*.bak_*
*.orig
*.rej
*~

# ============ Editor swap files ============
*.swp
*.swo
.*.swp

# ============ Editors / IDEs ============
.vscode/
.idea/
*.sublime-project
*.sublime-workspace
compile_commands.json
.cache/

# ============ OS cruft ============
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ============ Runtime state (engine writes at startup) ============
# status/ dirs contain engine.cfg, scene.dat — regenerated
status/

# ============ Logs ============
# fix_log.txt IS tracked (execution history). Only stray logs ignored.
!v15R3/v03_gate_validation.log
*.log

# ============ Sanitizer / temp build artifacts ============
/tmp/
temp/
*.san

# Keep the Python test harness itself versioned despite the broad C artifact
# pattern above; discard only interpreter cache files.
!tools/tests/*.py
# Same reasoning for the MFS suite, which `test_*` above silently excluded:
# tests/test_bounce_debug.c is a real source file, tracked by the standalone
# tree, and present here only as an untracked working-tree copy. A fresh clone
# of 475 lost it while 461 kept it -- a drift `sync_mfs_check.sh` cannot see,
# because it compares working trees and both had the file. It is part of the
# shared set the sync contract governs, so it must be versioned on both sides.
!v15S/src/ecosystem/mfs/tests/test_*.c
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# reference_materials/ : third-party papers (Mirtich, Baraff, Catto, Gottschalk,
# Coumans, Schmidl, Anitescu, Teschner). ~18 MB of COPYRIGHTED material that
# must not be pushed to a public repository. They are the authorities the
# validation doc cites; fetch them from the publishers and drop them here:
#   collision_detection/  Gottschalk OBBTree 1996; Coumans CCD 2005;
#                        Schmidl FastImpulseContactSuite 2004;
#                        vandenBergen ProximityQueries
#   constraint_solvers/  Anitescu fixed-timestep; Catto GDC 2005/2011/2013
#   impulse_simulation/  Mirtich 1995 + PhD thesis 1996
#   spatial_hashing/     Teschner GDC 2003
#   textbooks_theses/    Baraff thesis
reference_materials/
